  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Express $5{log}_{3}⁡4+5{log}_{3}⁡5$ as a single logarithm.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the product rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡a+{log}_{n}⁡b={log}_{n}⁡(ab)\n$$\n\nIf we factor the given expression and use the product rule for logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{log}_{3}⁡4+5{log}_{3}⁡5 & =5({log}_{3}⁡4+{log}_{3}⁡5) \\\\  & =5{log}_{3}⁡(4\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =5{log}_{3}⁡20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n5{log}_{3}⁡4+5{log}_{3}⁡5=5{log}_{3}⁡20.\n$$",
